actual_end_year = 1845
date_type = 1
edits_description = "The background was removed and the face was recolored."
final_image_tex = SubResource("Resource_gl4gq")
province = 70
blurb = "Depicts Yojirō, a monkey trainer from the play [url=https://www.kabuki21.com/horikawa.php]Chikagoro Kawara no Tatehiki (\"Recent Riverbed Confrontation\")[/url], seated by a smoking fire and a meal tray.

A tiny monkey can be seen in top right corner above the cartouche, as this print is from a series likening characters to zodiac animals.

The play is a love story between Yojirō's sister, a courtesan, and her lover, as well as Yojirō's devotion to his sister. The play was originally made for bunraku (puppet theater), but was later adapted to kabuki. The inscription in the top left praises Yojirō for his devotion.

One production of the play during the Meiji period used a real monkey, and ended up with said monkey urinating on stage."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://6kpsqyb2pk7a"
